{
  "configuration": "Same Rust 1.95.0 toolchain, native dev opt-level=z, release guest opt-level=z/LTO/one codegen unit. Identical test and adapter instrumentation. Fresh Core Schema bootstrap per version; local rendezvous; one agent; full storage authority; publishing/gossip disabled. Sequential runs after builds complete. Five direct get_holon_by_id Dance requests followed by five direct query_relationships requests (HolonSpace.HolonType / DescribedBy), each over authenticated AppWebsocket. Relationship results checked against the expected target ID. Every sample retained; no exclusions.",
  "limitations": "Single conductor per version and five samples per operation: directional evidence, not production percentiles. Required version-specific dependencies/API adaptations retained. Adapter interval starts inside dance_adapter after argument deserialization and ends after session export, before final logging, return construction/destruction and generated response serialization. Residual includes these plus client/conductor/VM/transport work. HDK costs and counts cover dispatch; nested components overlap and must not be added to adapter or complete-call totals. Complete call surrounds AppWebsocket.call_zome, excluding external envelope encoding/decoding; logical call surrounds context.initiate_dance and includes session handling. Production behavior/caching unchanged.",
